    "created_at": "2022-10-27T08:54:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-27T08:54:15Z",
    "body": "Thx for the explanation @annevk . I guess that makes sense in the browser context. Doesn't that mean that the SSE thing should be deprecated then? or whatever EOL process you have for it?\r\n\r\nIt's unfortunate the spec is part of WHATWG, since I'm running into it in an IOT environment, where the simplicity of the spec is really useful. Especially resource constraint devices (typically not even capable of TLS), will not be able to implement the stream/fetch apis, yet they mostly do have a simple http engine. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
