    "created_at": "2022-10-27T09:04:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-27T09:04:29Z",
    "body": "The web doesn't really do EOL unless there's security or privacy problems, or something is so severely broken everyone agrees it pays to break compatibility.\r\n\r\nWe don't really have a convention for indicating things are solely being maintained (e.g., this also applies to `XMLHttpRequest`), but maybe we should have.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
